"""Individual pattern mechanisms, costs, and language-neutral miniature implementations."""
PATTERN_LESSONS={
4:[
('Factory Method','A creator varies the product it constructs through an overridable or supplied creation operation. A report exporter can ask make_writer() without selecting a concrete writer in its processing skeleton. Use it when construction is a meaningful variation point; a plain injected function is often enough. It differs from Abstract Factory, which creates a compatible family. Avoid inheritance merely to rename a constructor.', ['Exporter calls factory method','Concrete creator selects CSV writer','Writer satisfies output contract'], 'export(rows):\n    writer = make_writer()\n    writer.write(rows)'),
('Abstract Factory','A family factory constructs mutually compatible collaborators, such as a renderer and template engine for one notification format. It prevents accidentally mixing incompatible families. It adds interfaces and can make introducing a new product kind expensive. Prefer direct construction when there is one stable family; choose it when clients genuinely switch whole families rather than only one implementation.', ['Select HTML family','Create HTML renderer and template','Both share compatible content model'], 'family = HtmlNotificationFactory()\nrenderer = family.renderer()\ntemplate = family.template()\nrenderer.render(template, data)'),
('Builder','A builder accumulates a complex construction request and validates it before creating a usable value. A notification can require recipient and template while allowing optional locale and expiry. Do not expose an invalid partially built notification as if ready. A direct constructor or named parameters is clearer for a small value. Unlike a factory family, the builder emphasizes staged assembly and validation.', ['Set recipient and template','Add optional expiry','Build validates required fields'], 'builder.to(recipient).template(template_id)\nnotification = builder.expires_at(deadline).build()\n# build rejects missing recipient or incompatible fields'),
('Prototype','A prototype creates an object by copying an existing configured instance. Copying a report layout can be convenient when configuration is expensive. Define shallow versus deep copy and ownership of shared resources; copying a connection handle does not create an independent connection. Prefer immutable shared configuration plus new per-request state when that makes aliasing clearer.', ['Configured layout prototype','Copy layout-owned values','Do not duplicate resource ownership'], 'layout = prototype.clone_owned_values()\nlayout.title = "Monthly report"\n# Shared immutable font data remains shared'),
('Singleton','A singleton restricts instance access within a specified program or container boundary. It is not globally unique across processes. Shared immutable configuration can be appropriate; shared mutable request state creates races and testing interference. Container-managed singleton lifetime and the classic global-access pattern are related but distinct. Prefer explicit injection and documented ownership so global access does not hide dependencies or prevent isolation.', ['Process A has instance S1','Process B has instance S2','Global uniqueness is not implied'], 'configuration = load_immutable_configuration()\nservice = Service(configuration)\n# One application-owned instance; no hidden global lookup')],
5:[
('Adapter','An adapter translates an existing interface or representation into the contract its client needs. A provider-specific SMS response becomes accepted, declined, or uncertain with a stable reference. Translation must preserve meaning, not only field names. Use it at a real interoperability boundary; avoid wrappers that expose the same volatile SDK types. Unlike Decorator, its principal intent is interface translation.', ['Application Sender contract','Translate request and outcomes','Foreign SMS provider API'], 'send(message):\n    raw = sdk.submit(encode(message))\n    return map_provider_outcome(raw)'),
('Bridge','A bridge separates two independent dimensions of variation, such as notification content types and delivery transports. Each content model uses a transport contract rather than subclassing every content-channel combination. It costs explicit composition and boundaries. It differs from Adapter, which usually reconciles an existing mismatch; Bridge deliberately designs independent variation before combinations multiply.', ['Alert or receipt content','Composes transport interface','Email or SMS transport'], 'class Receipt:\n    constructor(transport): self.transport = transport\n    deliver(data): return self.transport.send(format_receipt(data))'),
('Composite','A composite exposes a compatible interface for leaves and groups. A notification audience may be a user or a group of audiences. Recursive traversal must define cycles, duplicates, failure aggregation, and size limits. Do not treat a group send as atomically successful just because it shares a method with a leaf. Prefer an ordinary collection loop when a tree-shaped structure does not clarify the domain.', ['Audience group contains audiences','Leaf is one authorized recipient','Traversal bounds and deduplicates'], 'recipients(node, seen):\n    if node.id in seen: return []\n    seen.add(node.id)\n    return node.users_or_recursive_children(seen)'),
('Decorator','A decorator preserves a collaborator interface while adding behavior around calls, such as metrics or formatting. Composition order matters: retry(metrics(sender)) counts attempts differently from metrics(retry(sender)). A retry decorator changes effect risk unless operations are safe under a stable identity contract. Use it for orthogonal behavior, not to bury business policy in an opaque stack. Unlike Adapter, it normally retains the same interface.', ['Metrics wraps Sender','Sender returns explicit outcome','Wrapper records duration and result'], 'send(message):\n    start = clock()\n    try: return inner.send(message)\n    finally: metrics.observe(clock() - start)'),
('Facade','A facade offers a focused entry point to a subsystem, such as submit_notification() coordinating validation, templating, and durable intent. It reduces the client’s need to understand subsystem details. It must not turn into an unbounded god object or conceal important asynchronous outcomes. Unlike a proxy, its main purpose is a simpler subsystem interface, not controlling access to an otherwise identical target.', ['Client uses one submit operation','Facade coordinates subsystem roles','Returns accepted intent identity'], 'submit(command):\n    validated = validate(command)\n    return intents.persist(render_plan(validated))'),
('Flyweight','A flyweight shares immutable intrinsic state while keeping per-use context external. Many rendered notifications can reuse one parsed template definition while each supplies a recipient and variables. Sharing mutable recipient state would leak data. Measure memory pressure before adding a pool or cache; ordinary immutable reuse can be sufficient. A flyweight does not automatically provide cache invalidation or lifetime management.', ['Shared immutable template parse','Recipient A context separate','Recipient B context separate'], 'template = parsed_templates.get(version)\noutput_a = render(template, context_a)\noutput_b = render(template, context_b)'),
('Proxy','A proxy implements a target interface while controlling access, placement, or initialization. An authorization proxy can check permission before forwarding a document read. Remote proxies must expose network uncertainty rather than pretending every local call is instant and reliable. Unlike a facade, it commonly stands in for the same conceptual target. Avoid a transparent-looking API that hides expensive retries or unbounded lazy loads.', ['Client requests document read','Proxy checks current access','Authorized target returns data'], 'read(document_id, actor):\n    authorize(actor, document_id)\n    return target.read(document_id)')],
6:[
('Strategy','A strategy supplies an interchangeable algorithm behind a stable behavioral contract, such as channel selection or fee calculation. It lets one algorithm vary without changing its caller. The strategies must agree on units, errors, and effect semantics. A single stable formula can be a function rather than a class hierarchy. Strategy differs from State because the variation is selected policy rather than lifecycle-dependent behavior.', ['Policy selects strategy','Caller invokes stable operation','Algorithm returns defined result'], 'price = pricing_strategy.calculate(order)\nrequire(price.currency == order.currency)'),
('Observer','An observer subscribes to notifications from a subject. Define synchronous versus asynchronous delivery, subscription lifetime, ordering, and exceptions. A local callback list is not a durable broker. A slow or failing observer can delay the subject if invoked inline; an unremoved observer can retain memory. Use for real one-to-many reactions, but use durable event publication when the reaction must survive a process crash.', ['Subject changes state','Subscribed observers notified','Failure policy defines isolation'], 'for observer in snapshot(subscribers):\n    notify_under_defined_failure_policy(observer, event)'),
('Command','A command represents an intention with explicit inputs and identity, enabling scheduling or audit. It differs from an event, which records a fact already accepted. A retryable command must define duplicate handling and validity at execution time. Capturing an arbitrary closure may retain invalid request resources and cannot automatically be persisted. Prefer serializable domain data and an explicit handler for durable work.', ['Command: send receipt','Queue stores versioned intention','Handler validates and executes'], 'command = SendReceipt(order_id, operation_id)\nhandler.handle(command)\n# Handler checks current authorization and state'),
('State','State objects or transition tables vary behavior by an entity lifecycle. A pending payment accepts settlement evidence; a refunded payment rejects shipment under the domain policy. Keep transitions and guards explicit and persist them atomically. One class per state is optional; a small transition table may be clearer. Unlike Strategy, current state is constrained by history and cannot be selected arbitrarily by a caller.', ['Pending payment','Verified settlement transition','Captured state permits refund request'], 'require((payment.state, event.kind) in allowed_transitions)\npayment.state = next_state(payment.state, event)'),
('Chain of Responsibility','A chain passes a request through ordered handlers that may handle, transform, reject, or forward it. Authentication, admission, and parsing middleware are common examples. Define termination and propagation rules so an omitted next() does not silently swallow work. Handler order can change security and cost. It differs from a workflow requiring every mandatory stage to commit; a chain alone supplies no durable progress or compensation.', ['Authenticate','Apply request budget','Parse and invoke next handler'], 'auth(rate_limit(parse(application)))(request)\n# Each handler has explicit rejection and continuation rules'),
('Template Method','A template method fixes an algorithm skeleton and permits selected steps to vary, commonly through inheritance. A base import job can enforce validate, transform, and commit order while formats customize transformation. The base class must preserve valid extension points. Strategy composition is often easier when several steps vary independently. Avoid inheritance that allows subclasses to skip the invariant-protecting skeleton entirely.', ['Fixed validate step','Overridable transform step','Fixed commit and cleanup'], 'run(input):\n    validate(input)\n    result = transform(input)\n    return commit(result)'),
('Iterator','An iterator exposes traversal without requiring clients to know the collection representation. Database cursors or paginated readers also carry lifetime, ordering, and resource contracts. A lazy iterator can hold a connection while a slow client waits; disposing its owner too early can break traversal. Define snapshot and mutation behavior. For small bounded results, a materialized list may be simpler and safer.', ['Client requests next item','Iterator owns traversal position','End or close releases resources'], 'with open_bounded_cursor(query) as rows:\n    for row in rows:\n        consume(row)'),
('Mediator','A mediator coordinates collaborators that would otherwise communicate through many direct relationships. A checkout coordinator can sequence inventory and payments while each remains focused. The mediator must have explicit state and failure behavior; otherwise it becomes a god object with hidden dependencies. A durable workflow orchestrator is one possible distributed extension, not a guarantee supplied by the object pattern itself.', ['Inventory reports reservation','Mediator decides next action','Payment collaborator receives command'], 'reservation = inventory.reserve(command)\noutcome = payments.authorize(command.operation_id)\ncoordinate_outcomes(reservation, outcome)'),
('Memento','A memento captures state for a supported restoration boundary without exposing arbitrary internals. An editor may snapshot local draft state for undo. Define what is included and whether references are copied safely. Restoring local memory cannot reverse a payment or erase a message already sent. Event history, compensations, and backups solve different problems. Use when state capture is manageable and restoration semantics are genuinely well defined.', ['Capture local draft snapshot','Apply editable change','Restore supported local state'], 'before = draft.snapshot_owned_values()\ndraft.apply(edit)\ndraft.restore(before)\n# No claim about undoing external effects'),
('Visitor','A visitor adds operations over a known structure by dispatching on element type. A document tree can support export, validation, or counting without placing every operation on every node. It eases adding operations but makes adding new element types more expensive because visitors must handle them. Prefer ordinary pattern matching when it is simpler in the language. Keep exhaustive handling and unknown-element behavior explicit during schema evolution.', ['Known document node variants','Visitor supplies export operation','Each node dispatches appropriate behavior'], 'visit(node):\n    match node.kind:\n        case "text": return export_text(node)\n        case "image": return export_image(node)\n        case _: raise UnsupportedNode')],
7:[
('Repository','A repository mediates domain-oriented persistence rather than exposing storage syntax everywhere. Its contract must define transactions, errors, query bounds, and returned-value lifetime. A repository per table is not always the right aggregate boundary. Do not hide slow remote calls or lazy resources behind a misleadingly cheap-looking method. Use it when it protects meaningful knowledge, while retaining real storage integration tests.', ['Domain operation','Repository contract','Concrete persistence adapter'], 'reservation = repository.get_for_update(reservation_id)\nreservation.confirm(payment_evidence)\nrepository.save(reservation)'),
('Unit of Work','A Unit of Work groups local changes under one commit and tracks their ownership. Inventory decrement and reservation insert can belong to one transaction. Commit and cleanup semantics must be explicit, and collaborators must not secretly commit independently. It cannot atomically include an unrelated payment provider simply because both are called inside a language scope. Keep the unit short and free of unnecessary network waits.', ['Begin local transaction','Apply related local changes','Commit both or roll back'], 'with unit_of_work() as uow:\n    uow.inventory.reserve(seat)\n    uow.reservations.add(record)\n    uow.commit()'),
('Specification','A specification names a reusable predicate or selection rule, such as eligible_for_refund(payment,now). Keep its semantics explicit when translating it into a database query, especially around nulls, time, and authorization. Reusing a pure predicate is simple; an elaborate expression framework is justified only by real composition needs. A specification describes eligibility, not the atomic transition that prevents eligibility from changing concurrently.', ['Evaluate refund predicate','Concurrent state may change','Atomic transition rechecks invariant'], 'eligible = RefundPolicy.satisfied_by(payment, now)\nif eligible:\n    repository.refund_if_still_eligible(payment.version)'),
('CQRS','Separate command and query models when they need different behavior or shape. A transaction-safe payment aggregate can emit changes to a read-friendly statement view. The read side can lag, so freshness and rebuilding must be specified. It need not use separate processes, storage engines, or event sourcing. Avoid the additional synchronization and model maintenance when one straightforward model already serves the workload.', ['Command enforces invariant','Projection updates read model','Query serves explicit freshness'], 'commands.capture(payment_id, operation_id)\nstatement = queries.account_statement(account_id)\n# Projection lag is part of the query contract')]
}
